.* LICPGM: GO LICPGM, the licensed program tasks, with IBM's option
.* numbers (docs/LICPGM.md §9).
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PANELID CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='LICPGM'.
:KEYL NAME=MENUKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F13 ACTION='MENU INFO'.F13=Information Assistant
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='MENU MAIN'.F16=System Main menu
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=LICPGM HELP=HLPLICPGM KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM PANELID=PANELID.Work with Licensed Programs
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUGRP.Manual Install
:MENUI OPTION=1 ACTION='CMD QSLICPGM OPTION(1)'.Install all
:EMENUGRP.
:MENUGRP.Preparation
:MENUI OPTION=5 ACTION='MENU LICPREP'.Prepare for install
:EMENUGRP.
:MENUGRP.Licensed Programs
:MENUI OPTION=10 ACTION='CMD QSLICPGM OPTION(10)'.Display installed licensed programs
:MENUI OPTION=11 ACTION='CMD QSLICPGM OPTION(11)'.Install licensed programs
:MENUI OPTION=12 ACTION='CMD QSLICPGM OPTION(12)'.Delete licensed programs
:MENUI OPTION=13 ACTION='CMD QSLICPGM OPTION(13)'.Save licensed programs
:EMENUGRP.
:MENUGRP.Secondary Languages
:MENUI OPTION=20 ACTION='CMD QSLICPGM OPTION(20)'.Display secondary languages
:MENUI OPTION=21 ACTION='CMD QSLICPGM OPTION(21)'.Install secondary languages
:MENUI OPTION=22 ACTION='CMD QSLICPGM OPTION(22)'.Delete secondary languages
:EMENUGRP.
:MENUGRP.Completion Status
:MENUI OPTION=50 ACTION='CMD DSPLOG'.Display log for messages
:EMENUGRP.
:MENUGRP.Related
:MENUI OPTION=70 ACTION='MENU CMDLIC'.Licensed program commands
:EMENUGRP.
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPLICPGM.Work with Licensed Programs - Help
:P.Install, display, delete and save the licensed programs, and their
language features. An install shows each product's software agreement
first; the product is installed once it is accepted.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
